/target
**/*.rs.bk
.env
scripts/__pycache__/

# Scratch: working files, scrape output and logs. Kept on disk, never in the
# repository — the one thing under it that a BUILD needs (the recall test key)
# lives beside its test at crates/tools/tests/data/answer-key.tsv.
scratch/

# **No local `.cargo/config.toml`, and never a committed one.** `rano` is a git
# dependency pinned to a tag, and unreleased rano work is built through a `[patch]`
# on the branch that needs it, dropped before the merge. A `paths = [...]` override
# here is the old arrangement and a trap: cargo swaps the dependency for the local
# checkout whatever version the lock asks for, so a checkout left at an old release
# breaks the build silently. MEASURED 2026-10-08 on the Linux box: a v0.2.1 checkout
# under a lock that wanted v0.6.0, and nothing that depends on crates/ui compiled.
# Still ignored, because an absolute path in a committed file is what made the
# daemon unbuildable on a runner.
/.cargo/config.toml
